    "result_text": "Build is green. Let me confirm the full picture is consistent \u2014 all four RFC7807 members are present for every rejection path.\n\nThe change is complete and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe gap was in `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleRejectedRequestException` \u2014 the handler for `RejectedRequestException`, which is the exception the owner-create flow throws for all the business-rule rejections (400 Bad Request, 409 Conflict, 429 Too Many Requests). It was returning:\n\n```java\nreturn ResponseEntity.status(status).build();   // status only, empty body\n```\n\nThat produced the correct HTTP status but no body at all \u2014 violating the spec's requirement that 400/409/429 rejections carry an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body.\n\nI changed it to build a `ProblemDetail` via the existing `detailBuild(...)` helper (the same one the other handlers use), so the response now carries all four required members:\n\n- `type` \u2014 the request URL\n- `title` \u2014 the exception class name\n- `status` \u2014 set by `ProblemDetail.forStatus(status)`, equal to the HTTP status\n- `detail` \u2014 the status reason phrase\n\n```java\nHttpStatus status = e.getStatus();\nlogger.warn(\"Request rejected at {} {} with status {}\",\n    request.getMethod(), request.getRequestURI(), status.value());\nProblemDetail detail = this.detailBuild(e, status, request.getRequestURL(), status.getReasonPhrase());\nreturn ResponseEntity.status(status).body(detail);\n```\n\nReturning a `ProblemDetail` body makes Spring serialize it as `application/problem+json` automatically (identical to the sibling handlers for `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, `DataIntegrityViolationException`, etc.), and the HTTP status codes are unchanged. The other two rejection handlers already returned proper problem+json bodies, so this brought the last path into line.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS** (`AcceptanceTest.coreRejectionIsProblemJson` passes, asserting the `application/problem+json` content type and `$.status == 400`).",
